# gjoa-patch:
#   baseline-firefox: 160.0
#   touches:
#     - Cargo.lock
#     - toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.cpp
#     - toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.h
#     - toolkit/components/content-classifier/nsIContentClassifierService.idl
#     - toolkit/components/content-classifier/moz.build
#     - toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/ContentClassifierEngine.cpp
#     - toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/ContentClassifierEngine.h
#     - toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/src/lib.rs
#     - toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/Cargo.toml
#
Extend the upstream content-classifier component with native cosmetic
element-hiding.

- Rust FFI: url_cosmetic_resources + hidden_class_id_selectors (+ fill_cstr_thinvec)
- IDL: getUrlCosmeticResources + getHiddenClassIdSelectors
- C++ engine wrappers + cross-engine union in the service
- Since Firefox 160 upstream registers @mozilla.org/content-classifier-service;1
  itself (GetInstance) and builds on the in-tree etp_engine fork of adblock-rust,
  so this patch no longer adds a contract; it only extends the engine + IDL.
- Rust: serde_json dep for the scriptlet resource library (setScriptletResources)
- moz.build: register the overlaid GjoaCosmetic{Parent,Child}.sys.mjs actors as
  EXTRA_JS_MODULES
